WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.570
A law to keep under-15s off social media.

2
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.270
In 2026, France's Parliament
votes for the ban,

3
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.760
with age checks for every user.

4
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.070
Then, in August, the ban is
stopped before it can take effect.

5
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.240
Supporters say «les plateformes sont
conçues pour capter l'attention».

6
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.880
Opponents reply: «Mieux
vaut éduquer qu'interdire».

7
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.720
So what stopped the ban,

8
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.300
and which side has the stronger case?

9
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.700
In this mission, you'll trace how France
tried to protect young people online,

10
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.300
step by step.

11
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.810
Then you'll argue both sides of the ban,

12
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:38.850
in French. Your mission: find
out what stopped the ban,

13
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.990
and decide who you think is right.
